 "growth_rationale": "Low-confidence estimate of 8% annual FCF growth, set between two conflicting signals. Historically FCF fell from $7.552B in 2022 to $6.220B in 2025 (about -6.3%/yr), while operating income fell about 65% and operating cash flow stayed flat at about $14.7B (MARKET DATA history). Capex is also rising: PP&E grew $6.6B in H1 2026 and Other non-current assets grew $4.4B (SEC 10-Q 2026-07-23). Against that, revenue is accelerating, up 21% in H1 2026 and with 12-13% consensus growth for 2026-27 (Yahoo Finance - Analysis). Consensus EPS growth for 2027 is 23%, but 2026 and 2027 EPS estimates were cut by about 16-18% over 90 days (Yahoo Finance - Analysis). Operating margin is only 1.4% in Q2 2026, and SBC exceeds operating income (SEC 10-Q 2026-07-23). I therefore assume only partial conversion of revenue growth into FCF. The H1 2026 cash flow statement is truncated in the material, so there is no current FCF run-rate to anchor this.",
