{"moat":{"rating":"narrow","sources_of_moat":["Supercharger network and NACS standard: a proprietary network that is now partly monetized through other OEMs' drivers. Its advantage is eroding as rival networks scale.","Fleet data and software: FSD is a data flywheel with a reported ~12B cumulative supervised miles and ~1.48M paid FSD subscriptions. It could become a strong moat, but unsupervised autonomy at scale is unproven.","Vertical integration (in-house battery cells, chips, giga-casting, direct sales): a real cost and iteration advantage, but recent margin compression suggests it does not guarantee pricing power.","Brand: strong with EV-native buyers, but CEO-related reputational headwinds in Western markets.","Energy storage scale (Megapack): growing quickly, but margins are volatile."],"evidence":"Mixed. Automotive gross margin ex-credits fell to 16.3% and energy gross margin dropped sharply in Q2 2026. Filings-based figures show FY2025 operating margin of 5.1% vs 17.0% in FY2022, which is hard to square with a wide moat. Management cited warranty charges, tariff changes, pricing and higher financing costs. Model 3 and Model Y made up 97% of deliveries. Tesla's share of global EV sales is only about 12-13%, and BYD delivered 557,090 BEVs in Q2 2026 against Tesla's 480,126. FSD paid subscriptions are up 56% YoY, and 55% of North American deliveries came with a subscription. Services and Other margin hit a record 14.1%. Third-party moat ratings differ: GuruFocus scores it 7/10, 'entry-level wide', while another analysis calls the tech lead 'defensible but narrowing' and pricing power 'materially diminished'. I rate it narrow because the autonomy and robotics moat is not yet evidenced in returns on capital. ROE is 4.67% per the market data."},"management":{"rating":"average","capital_allocation":"Tesla is in a heavy investment cycle. CapEx is expected to exceed $25B in 2026 and rise further over the next few years. Q2 free cash flow was about -$1.1B as capex doubled sequentially. Management is lining up up to $30B of borrowing capacity. The CEO's stated approach is to spend as quickly as possible without being wasteful. Spending targets Robotaxi, Optimus, semiconductors, AI compute and a lithium/cathode refinery. These bets are large, long-dated and have no disclosed return hurdles, so ROIC is unknown. Per the filings summary, Q2 R&D rose ~49% and SG&A ~45%, and Q2 stock-based compensation was $1.22B vs $0.69B a year earlier. Share count rose from ~3.75B (Jan 2026 cover) to ~3.95B (Jul 2026 cover); the cause is not confirmed in my sources. There are no buybacks or dividends. The balance sheet is strong at $43.5B of cash and investments against ~$9.3B of debt per the 10-Q. Operating execution is mixed: record deliveries and a record order backlog, but EPS missed and margins fell. <cite index=\"4-4\">Q2 revenue was $28.24B vs a $25.55B estimate, and adjusted EPS of $0.33 missed the $0.49 forecast.</cite> Overall, management is ambitious and operationally capable, but capital discipline is unproven.","governance_concerns":["Board independence: <cite index=\"19-13\">A Delaware judge found the board too close to Musk to negotiate his pay at arm's length.</cite> <cite index=\"19-14\">Electrek says that board dynamic has not changed.</cite>","Pay package: <cite index=\"19-1\">On April 21, 2026 the board signed an implementation agreement to deliver the 2018 award and revoked the $29B interim package.</cite> <cite index=\"19-2\">Tesla registered 304M shares for it, now worth over $114B.</cite> <cite index=\"19-10\">$9.97B of unrecognized stock-based compensation expense will hit earnings.</cite>","<cite index=\"22-5\">In Nov 2025 the board approved a ~$1T equity-based package for Musk.</cite> <cite index=\"22-6\">It would raise his ownership to ~29%.</cite> <cite index=\"24-1\">ISS advised shareholders to reject it.</cite> <cite index=\"24-4\">ISS said it has no explicit requirement to keep Musk's time and attention on Tesla.</cite>","Key-person and distraction risk: <cite index=\"24-3\">Musk oversees five companies: Tesla, SpaceX, xAI, Neuralink and the Boring Company.</cite>","Dilution and rising SBC will weigh on per-share returns.","Brand and political risk linked to the CEO."]},"industry":{"growth_outlook":"Global EV demand is still growing, but at a slower pace. <cite index=\"29-1\">The IEA says 2025 electric car sales grew 20% to exceed 20M.</cite> <cite index=\"32-1\">EV Volumes estimates 2026 global EV sales of 22.7M, up only modestly from 2025.</cite> <cite index=\"30-4\">Counterpoint says BEVs were 19% of Q2 2026 passenger car sales, with BEV sales up 24% YoY.</cite> Tesla's analyst-consensus revenue growth is ~12-13% a year for 2026-27 (Yahoo, per the filings summary). The larger upside is the option value in robotaxi, FSD subscriptions, energy storage and humanoid robots, none of which is proven at scale. The US faces a headwind from expired federal EV tax credits.","competitive_intensity":"High and rising. Chinese overcapacity is being exported; <cite index=\"31-2\">China produces well over half of the world's EVs and batteries.</cite> <cite index=\"32-10\">Competition is shifting from rapid expansion to aggressive share capture.</cite> BYD led annual BEV sales in 2025 (<cite index=\"32-8\">2.26M vs Tesla's 1.64M</cite>). Legacy OEMs have adopted the Tesla charging connector, which weakens Tesla's charging edge. In autonomy, Tesla faces Waymo and others.","key_competitors":["BYD","Geely/Zeekr","Volkswagen Group","GM","Ford","Toyota","Hyundai/Kia","Xiaomi","XPeng","NIO","Li Auto","Rivian","Lucid","Waymo (robotaxi)","Baidu Apollo Go (robotaxi; not confirmed in sources)"]},"catalysts":["Unsupervised Robotaxi expansion: <cite index=\"6-3\">operations in seven metros</cite>, with Phoenix and Las Vegas next.","Cybercab production ramp: <cite index=\"3-3\">production began in Q2 2026.</cite>","Optimus production start; <cite index=\"7-7\">management said it will soon start Optimus production.</cite>","FSD approvals in Europe: <cite index=\"6-3\">approvals so far in the Netherlands, Lithuania, Estonia, Denmark and Belgium</cite>; FSD V14-Lite rollout to AI3 vehicles.","Energy storage: <cite index=\"9-4\">13.5 GWh deployed in Q2, up 41% YoY</cite>; Megapack 3 production soon.","Margin recovery or further decline in auto gross margin, warranty and tariff effects; trajectory of free cash flow given capex above $25B.","Next earnings report (Q3 2026) and delivery data.","Resolution of CEO pay and governance issues, and dilution from the Musk award."],"citations":["https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/tesla-q2-earnings-call-highlights-2026-07-22/","https://www.gurufocus.com/news/8973433/tesla-inc-tsla-q2-2026-earnings-call-highlights-record-deliveries-and-strategic-investments-amid-margin-pressures","https://www.notateslaapp.com/news/4481/summary-of-teslas-2026-q2-earnings-call-cybercab-fsd-ai4-and-more","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/TSLA/pressreleases/3667292/tesla-tsla-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/05/tesla-tsla-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.investing.com/news/transcripts/earnings-call-transcript-tesla-q2-2026-revenue-beats-eps-misses-as-stock-falls-93CH-4807216","https://www.shacknews.com/article/150109/tesla-tsla-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript","https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/TSLA/earnings/TSLA-Q2-2026-earnings_call-653184.html","https://www.gurufocus.com/term/moat-score/TSLA","https://norrisai.us/analysis/tsla-q2-2026/","https://electrek.co/2026/04/27/tesla-files-deliver-elon-musk-56-billion-pay-package-shares/","https://fortune.com/2025/10/17/tesla-shareholders-should-reject-musks-1-trillion-pay-package-iss-advises","https://poole.ncsu.edu/thought-leadership/article/inside-the-implications-of-musks-massive-deal/","https://www.iea.org/reports/global-ev-outlook-2026/trends-in-electric-cars","https://electriccarsreport.com/2026/07/byd-overtakes-tesla-again-in-q2-2026-ev-sales-as-global-gap-widens/","https://www.technobaboy.com/2026/08/28/tesla-byd-geely-lead-global-ev-market-in-q2-2026/","https://recharged.com/articles/electric-car-market-trends-2026/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001318605/000162828026049213/exhibit991.htm"]}
