asic / diluted","value":"3,237M / 3,540M","period":"Q2 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"metric":"Stock-based compensation","value":"$1,222M (Q2 2026) vs $692M (Q2 2025); $2,315M (H1 2026) vs $1,354M (H1 2025)","period":"Q2 and H1 2026","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23), statement of equity"},{"metric":"Automotive regulatory credits","value":"$146M vs $439M (Q2); $526M vs $1,034M (H1)","period":"Q2 and H1 2026 vs 2025","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"metric":"Energy segment gross margin (derived)","value":"20.4% vs 30.3%","period":"Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025","source":"Derived from SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"metric":"Cash and equivalents + short-term investments","value":"$15,219M + $28,305M = $43,524M (Dec 2025: $44,059M)","period":"2026-06-30","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23); MARKET DATA totalCash matches"},{"metric":"Debt and finance leases","value":"$1,418M current + $7,924M non-current = $9,342M (Dec 2025: $8,376M)","period":"2026-06-30","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23); sum derived"},{"metric":"Total debt per market data","value":"$16.08B (does not reconcile to the 10-Q balance sheet debt line)","period":"Current","source":"MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Total stockholders' equity; total assets","value":"$86,858M; $148,524M","period":"2026-06-30","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"metric":"PP&E, net; Other non-current assets","value":"$47,255M (Dec 2025: $40,643M); $9,453M (Dec 2025: $5,045M)","period":"2026-06-30","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"metric":"Derived EV and FCF multiples","value":"EV about $1.465T (mkt cap + $16.08B debt - $43.524B cash); EV/FY2025 FCF about 235x; FCF yield on market cap about 0.42%","period":"Current / FY2025","source":"Derived from MARKET DATA"},{"metric":"Consensus revenue","value":"$106.59B (2026, +12.41%); $120.48B (2027, +13.03%); 40 analysts","period":"FY2026E-FY2027E","source":"Yahoo Finance - Analysis"},{"metric":"Consensus EPS (basis not stated)","value":"$1.74 (2026); $2.14 (2027). 90 days ago: $2.11 and $2.56","period":"FY2026E-FY2027E","source":"Yahoo Finance - Analysis"},{"metric":"EPS earnings history on Yahoo","value":"Q2 FY26 actual $0.33 vs est. $0.54 (-39.15%); Q1 FY26 actual $0.41 vs est. $0.35","period":"Q1-Q2 2026","source":"Yahoo Finance - Analysis"}],"recommended_base_growth_rate":0.08,"growth_rationale":"Low-confidence estimate of 8% annual FCF growth, set between two conflicting signals. Historically FCF fell from $7.552B in 2022 to $6.220B in 2025 (about -6.3%/yr), while operating income fell about 65% and operating cash flow stayed flat at about $14.7B (MARKET DATA history). Capex is also rising: PP&E grew $6.6B in H1 2026 and Other non-current assets grew $4.4B (SEC 10-Q 2026-07-23). Against that, revenue is accelerating, up 21% in H1 2026 and with 12-13% consensus growth for 2026-27 (Yahoo Finance - Analysis). Consensus EPS growth for 2027 is 23%, but 2026 and 2027 EPS estimates were cut by about 16-18% over 90 days (Yahoo Finance - Analysis). Operating margin is only 1.4% in Q2 2026, and SBC exceeds operating income (SEC 10-Q 2026-07-23). I therefore assume only partial conversion of revenue growth into FCF. The H1 2026 cash flow statement is truncated in the material, so there is no current FCF run-rate to anchor this.","growth_sources":["MARKET DATA history (FCF, OCF, capex, operating income, revenue, FY2022-FY2025)","SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23): Q2/H1 2026 income statement and balance sheet","Yahoo Finance - Analysis: consensus revenue and EPS estimates and revisions"],"stated_risks":["The 10-K excerpt is truncated before Item 1A, so the full risk-factor text is not available. Only the forward-looking-statement language is available: supply chain constraints, competition, future operations and production capacity, projected costs and expected cost reductions, capital adequacy, demand and acceptance for the company's technologies, and growth opportunities (SEC 10-K 2026-01-29; SEC 10-Q 2026-07-23).","The 10-Q states that actual results may differ materially and refers readers to Item 1A of the FY2025 10-K and other SEC filings (SEC 10-Q 2026-07-23).","Analyst estimate revisions are skewed downward: 3 down vs 1 up over the last 7 days for the current quarter, and 4 down vs 1 up over 30 days for FY2026 (Yahoo Finance - Analysis). This is market sentiment, not a company-stated risk."],"accounting_red_flags":[{"flag":"Unexplained share-count jump with minimal recorded proceeds","evidence":"Shares outstanding rose from 3,752,431,984 (Jan 23, 2026) to 3,949,547,394 (Jul 16, 2026), about +197M or +5.3%. The equity statement shows 198M shares issued in H1 2026 and 194M in Q2 alone, 'for equity incentive awards and acquisitions', recorded at only $684M (H1) and $323M (Q2). That is under $2 per share against a price of about $378. The excerpt does not explain what was issued or why proceeds were so small.","source":"SEC 10-K (2026-01-29); SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"flag":"Large gap between outstanding shares and weighted-average shares","evidence":"Q2 2026 basic weighted average shares are 3,237M and diluted 3,540M, versus 3,949M outstanding (3,755M at Mar 31, 2026). Roughly 700M issued shares are not in basic EPS. The excerpt does not say why (for example, unvested restricted stock). XBRL tags reference CEO restricted stock and performance awards, but their terms are not in the excerpt. Market cap and P/B use 3.95B shares, while GAAP EPS uses about 3.2-3.5B, so per-share valuation is sensitive to the denominator.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23); MARKET DATA"},{"flag":"Pre-tax income depends heavily on non-operating items","evidence":"Q2 2026 income from operations was $398M, but pre-tax income was $1,329M. Interest income $422M, interest expense $(81)M and Other income, net $590M add $931M, about 70% of pre-tax income. Other income, net was $55M for H1, which implies about -$535M in Q1 (derived). The composition of 'Other income, net' (for example digital-asset or investment marks) is not disclosed in the excerpt. Digital assets fell from $1,008M to $674M over H1.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"flag":"Stock-based compensation exceeds operating profit","evidence":"SBC was $1,222M in Q2 2026 against operating income of $398M (3.1x). H1 SBC was $2,315M against operating income of $1,339M (1.7x). SBC rose 77% in Q2 year over year (from $692M).","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"flag":"Operating expenses growing faster than revenue; margin compression","evidence":"Q2 revenue was +25.5% year over year, but R&D was +49% and SG&A +45%. Operating margin fell to 1.4% from 4.1%. FY operating margin fell from 17.0% (2022) to 5.1% (2025).","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23); MARKET DATA history"},{"flag":"Declining high-margin credit revenue and falling energy margin","evidence":"Regulatory credits were $146M in Q2 2026 vs $439M, and $526M in H1 vs $1,034M. Energy gross margin was about 20.4% vs 30.3% (derived). Services and other gross margin is about 14.1% (derived).","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"flag":"Big unexplained balance-sheet build-up; possible related-party and AI/space exposure","evidence":"In six months, PP&E rose $6.6B (+16%) and Other non-current assets rose $4.4B (+87%, $5,045M to $9,453M). Inventory rose $1.4B, Accounts payable $2.0B (+14.6%) and Accrued liabilities $2.0B (+14.9%). XBRL contexts reference a SpaceX equity investment, a SpaceX March 2026 item, an 'AI hardware company', related-party activity, and a subsequent event with X.AI Holdings Corp. (10-K). The text, amounts and terms are not in the excerpts. The cash flow statement is truncated, so the funding and cash impact cannot be verified.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23); SEC 10-K (2026-01-29)"},{"flag":"Cash cushion shrinking while debt rises","evidence":"Cash plus short-term investments fell from $44,059M to $43,524M in H1 2026 despite stock issuance. Debt and finance leases rose from $8,376M to $9,342M. XBRL tags suggest a new warehouse line of credit in Q1 2026; terms are not in the excerpt.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"flag":"Net income vs operating income anomaly in FY2023 and weak FY2025 earnings quality","evidence":"FY2023 net income ($14.999B) exceeded operating income ($8.891B) by $6.1B, and the cause is not in the material. FY2025 FCF ($6.22B) was 164% of net income ($3.794B), while operating income fell 65% from FY2022 and OCF stayed flat. This suggests cash flow is supported by non-cash charges (SBC, D&A) and working capital. The cash flow statement breakdown is not provided.","source":"MARKET DATA history"},{"flag":"Settlement credited to equity","evidence":"'Shareholder settlement, net of tax' added $89M to APIC in H1 2026 ($27M tax) and $110M in H1 2025, bypassing the income statement. The nature of the settlement is not described in the excerpt.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"flag":"Vendor/consensus EPS is on a different basis than GAAP","evidence":"Yahoo lists Q1 FY26 actual EPS of $0.41, but implied Q1 GAAP diluted EPS is about $0.13 (H1 $0.45 less Q2 $0.32 from the 10-Q). Consensus 2026 EPS of $1.74 compares with H1 GAAP EPS of $0.45. Forward P/E of 176x (implies EPS of about $2.14, equal to the 2027 estimate) is probably on an adjusted basis, so adjustments such as SBC are not confirmed.","source":"Yahoo Finance - Analysis; SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23); MARKET DATA"},{"flag":"Market-data debt does not reconcile to the filing","evidence":"MARKET DATA totalDebt is $16.08B, while the 10-Q balance sheet shows $9,342M of debt and finance leases. The difference may be operating leases, but that is not confirmed. totalCash of $43.524B does reconcile ($15,219M + $28,305M).","source":"MARKET DATA; SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"},{"flag":"Effective tax rate volatility","evidence":"Q2 2026 provision was $201M on $1,329M pre-tax income (15.1%) vs $359M on $1,549M (23.2%) in Q2 2025. The H1 2026 rate was 22.1%. The reason for the Q2 decline is not given in the excerpt.","source":"SEC 10-Q (2026-07-23)"}],"data_gaps":["The 10-K text after the cover, forward-looking statements and index is missing (Item 1 business, Item 1A risk factors, MD&A, notes), so the full list of stated risks is unavailable.","The 10-Q cash flow statement is truncated, so H1 2026 operating cash flow, capex, FCF, D&A and working-capital changes are unavailable. The latest FCF figure is FY2025 from MARKET DATA.","No 10-Q notes or MD&A are provided: nature of the 'Other income, net', 'acquisitions' share issuance, the SpaceX/AI-hardware/X.AI items, debt terms and the warehouse line, and the settlement are all undisclosed.","The reason for the roughly 700M gap between outstanding and weighted-average shares, and the exact share count (basic, diluted, or incl. unvested awards) to use for valuation, is not documented.","Reconciliation of MARKET DATA totalDebt ($16.08B) to the balance sheet ($9.342B) is not provided.","Management guidance and segment-level profitability (operating income by segment) are not provided.","Analyst consensus covers revenue and EPS only. There are no FCF, capex or margin forecasts, and the GAAP/non-GAAP basis of the EPS estimates is not clear on the Yahoo page, which loaded with an 'Oops, something went wrong' message.","Peer or industry benchmarks are not provided.","Quarterly FCF history and TTM FCF to mid-2026 are not provided."]}
Qualitative: {"moat":{"rating":"narrow","sources_of_moat":["Supercharger network and NACS standard: a proprietary network that is now partly monetized through other OEMs' drivers. Its advantage is eroding as rival networks scale.","Fleet data and software: FSD is a data flywheel with a reported ~12B cumulative supervised miles and ~1.48M paid FSD subscriptions. It could become a strong moat, but unsupervised autonomy at scale is unproven.","Vertical integration (in-house battery cells, chips, giga-casting, direct sales): a real cost and iteration advantage, but recent margin compression suggests it does not guarantee pricing power.","Brand: strong with EV-native buyers, but CEO-related reputational headwinds in Western markets.","Energy storage scale (Megapack): growing quickly, but margins are volatile."],"evidence":"Mixed. Automotive gross margin ex-credits fell to 16.3% and energy gross margin dropped sharply in Q2 2026. Filings-based figures show FY2025 operating margin of 5.1% vs 17.0% in FY2022, which is hard to square with a wide moat. Management cited warranty charges, tariff changes, pricing and higher financing costs. Model 3 and Model Y made up 97% of deliveries. Tesla's share of global EV sales is only about 12-13%, and BYD delivered 557,090 BEVs in Q2 2026 against Tesla's 480,126. FSD paid subscriptions are up 56% YoY, and 55% of North American deliveries came with a subscription. Services and Other margin hit a record 14.1%. Third-party moat ratings differ: GuruFocus scores it 7/10, 'entry-level wide', while another analysis calls the tech lead 'defensible but narrowing' and pricing power 'materially diminished'. I rate it narrow because the autonomy and robotics moat is not yet evidenced in returns on capital. ROE is 4.67% per the market data."},"management":{"rating":"average","capital_allocation":"Tesla is in a heavy investment cycle. CapEx is expected to exceed $25B in 2026 and rise further over the next few years. Q2 free cash flow was about -$1.1B as capex doubled sequentially. Management is lining up up to $30B of borrowing capacity. The CEO's stated approach is to spend as quickly as possible without being wasteful. Spending targets Robotaxi, Optimus, semiconductors, AI compute and a lithium/cathode refinery. These bets are large, long-dated and have no disclosed return hurdles, so ROIC is unknown. Per the filings summary, Q2 R&D rose ~49% and SG&A ~45%, and Q2 stock-based compensation was $1.22B vs $0.69B a year earlier. Share count rose from ~3.75B (Jan 2026 cover) to ~3.95B (Jul 2026 cover); the cause is not confirmed in my sources. There are no buybacks or dividends. The balance sheet is strong at $43.5B of cash and investments against ~$9.3B of debt per the 10-Q. Operating execution is mixed: record deliveries and a record order backlog, but EPS missed and margins fell. <cite index=\"4-4\">Q2 revenue was $28.24B vs a $25.55B estimate, and adjusted EPS of $0.33 missed the $0.49 forecast.</cite> Overall, management is ambitious and operationally capable, but capital discipline is unproven.","governance_concerns":["Board independence: <cite index=\"19-13\">A Delaware judge found the board too close to Musk to negotiate his pay at arm's length.</cite> <cite index=\"19-14\">Electrek says that board dynamic has not changed.</cite>","Pay package: <cite index=\"19-1\">On April 21, 2026 the board signed an implementation agreement to deliver the 2018 award and revoked the $29B interim package.</cite> <cite index=\"19-2\">Tesla registered 304M shares for it, now worth over $114B.</cite> <cite index=\"19-10\">$9.97B of unrecognized stock-based compensation expense will hit earnings.</cite>","<cite index=\"22-5\">In Nov 2025 the board approved a ~$1T equity-based package for Musk.</cite> <cite index=\"22-6\">It would raise his ownership to ~29%.</cite> <cite index=\"24-1\">ISS advised shareholders to reject it.</cite> <cite index=\"24-4\">ISS said it has no explicit requirement to keep Musk's time and attention on Tesla.</cite>","Key-person and distraction risk: <cite index=\"24-3\">Musk oversees five companies: Tesla, SpaceX, xAI, Neuralink and the Boring Company.</cite>","Dilution and rising SBC will weigh on per-share returns.","Brand and political risk linked to the CEO."]},"industry":{"growth_outlook":"Global EV demand is still growing, but at a slower pace. <cite index=\"29-1\">The IEA says 2025 electric car sales grew 20% to exceed 20M.</cite> <cite index=\"32-1\">EV Volumes estimates 2026 global EV sales of 22.7M, up only modestly from 2025.</cite> <cite index=\"30-4\">Counterpoint says BEVs were 19% of Q2 2026 passenger car sales, with BEV sales up 24% YoY.</cite> Tesla's analyst-consensus revenue growth is ~12-13% a year for 2026-27 (Yahoo, per the filings summary). The larger upside is the option value in robotaxi, FSD subscriptions, energy storage and humanoid robots, none of which is proven at scale. The US faces a headwind from expired federal EV tax credits.","competitive_intensity":"High and rising. Chinese overcapacity is being exported; <cite index=\"31-2\">China produces well over half of the world's EVs and batteries.</cite> <cite index=\"32-10\">Competition is shifting from rapid expansion to aggressive share capture.</cite> BYD led annual BEV sales in 2025 (<cite index=\"32-8\">2.26M vs Tesla's 1.64M</cite>). Legacy OEMs have adopted the Tesla charging connector, which weakens Tesla's charging edge. In autonomy, Tesla faces Waymo and others.","key_competitors":["BYD","Geely/Zeekr","Volkswagen Group","GM","Ford","Toyota","Hyundai/Kia","Xiaomi","XPeng","NIO","Li Auto","Rivian","Lucid","Waymo (robotaxi)","Baidu Apollo Go (robotaxi; not confirmed in sources)"]},"catalysts":["Unsupervised Robotaxi expansion: <cite index=\"6-3\">operations in seven metros</cite>, with Phoenix and Las Vegas next.","Cybercab production ramp: <cite index=\"3-3\">production began in Q2 2026.</cite>","Optimus production start; <cite index=\"7-7\">management said it will soon start Optimus production.</cite>","FSD approvals in Europe: <cite index=\"6-3\">approvals so far in the Netherlands, Lithuania, Estonia, Denmark and Belgium</cite>; FSD V14-Lite rollout to AI3 vehicles.","Energy storage: <cite index=\"9-4\">13.5 GWh deployed in Q2, up 41% YoY</cite>; Megapack 3 production soon.","Margin recovery or further decline in auto gross margin, warranty and tariff effects; trajectory of free cash flow given capex above $25B.","Next earnings report (Q3 2026) and delivery data.","Resolution of CEO pay and governance issues, and dilution from the Musk award."],"citations":["https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/tesla-q2-earnings-call-highlights-2026-07-22/","https://www.gurufocus.com/news/8973433/tesla-inc-tsla-q2-2026-earnings-call-highlights-record-deliveries-and-strategic-investments-amid-margin-pressures","https://www.notateslaapp.com/news/4481/summary-of-teslas-2026-q2-earnings-call-cybercab-fsd-ai4-and-more","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/TSLA/pressreleases/3667292/tesla-tsla-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/05/tesla-tsla-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.investing.com/news/transcripts/earnings-call-transcript-tesla-q2-2026-revenue-beats-eps-misses-as-stock-falls-93CH-4807216","https://www.shacknews.com/article/150109/tesla-tsla-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript","https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/TSLA/earnings/TSLA-Q2-2026-earnings_call-653184.html","https://www.gurufocus.com/term/moat-score/TSLA","https://norrisai.us/analysis/tsla-q2-2026/","https://electrek.co/2026/04/27/tesla-files-deliver-elon-musk-56-billion-pay-package-shares/","https://fortune.com/2025/10/17/tesla-shareholders-should-reject-musks-1-trillion-pay-package-iss-advises","https://poole.ncsu.edu/thought-leadership/article/inside-the-implications-of-musks-massive-deal/","https://www.iea.org/reports/global-ev-outlook-2026/trends-in-electric-cars","https://electriccarsreport.com